{
  "_readme": [
    "An example ~/.tvbox/firetv_ir_plan.json, keyed by the remote's MAC (lowercase).",
    "The UI normally writes this file from the published code index; this hand-written",
    "form exists because the index carries a device's four PROGRAMMABLE keys plus the",
    "input keys, and a box may be running against an index built before the input keys",
    "were published. Every code below is quoted from irdb and Flipper-IRDB.",
    "",
    "`assign` is deliberately empty: it says what the remote's own BUTTONS do, and this",
    "file is here for BLASTS - codes sent bound to no button at all, which is the only",
    "way to reach a TV input (CEC has no command that selects a foreign input) or a",
    "soundbar that is not on the CEC bus. Set config.ir.backend to \"firetv\" and point",
    "each action at a `<kind>:<Key>` target from below.",
    "",
    "The LG discrete socket codes are double-sourced (irdb LG/TV/4,-1.csv and the",
    "Flipper LG_MKJ39170828_Service.ir capture agree byte for byte at address 4, which",
    "is the address this TV's measured Power/Volume/Mute already sit on) - but their",
    "provenance is a service remote plus a crowd-sourced CSV, NOT a capture from a",
    "retail 2019 remote. Real LG consumer remotes carry only the stepping Input button",
    "(0x0B), so `Input` is the code most likely to work and the discrete ones are the",
    "prize. Try Input first, then HDMI2."
  ],
